{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nThe generated artifacts from a rebar-janitor session were lost. Reconstruct the recoverable results from `~/Downloads/ChatGPT-Rebar janitor analysis-20260816-0915.md`. Decisions 1-6 require the deepest research and analysis. This is a no-code recovery: preserve evidence, distinguish transcript facts from present-day corroboration, and make uncertainty explicit.\n\nThe current skill names `.rebar-janitor/`, but this repository’s historical local-only artifact convention is `.joe-janitor/`, evidenced by tracked `.joe-janitor/tools.md` and tracker record `naive-bigheaded-wildcat`. Other git-excluded files visible in one checkout are opportunistic corroboration only: the plan does not assume that `known-fine.md` or prior `report-*.md` files survive. The deterministic output is `.joe-janitor/report-2026-08-16-recovered.md`. Its title and opening banner must say `RECOVERED — NOT A NATIVE JANITOR RUN` so future runs cannot mistake reconstructed material for an original Phase-2 record.\n\n## Plan\n- Inventory the source transcript, its structure, and any surviving repository/tracker evidence without modifying production code.\n- Identify the rebar-janitor protocol version in effect during the transcript from its content and repository history; use the current protocol as a guide, labeling inferred mappings if the historical structure differs.\n- Reconstruct the Phase 1/2 finding and verification context needed to interpret the later decisions.\n- Recover decisions 1-6 individually, tracing evidence, prior decisions, competing remediation proposals, convergence/divergence, approval state, and ticketization status where available.\n- Cross-check material claims against the repository, ADRs, commit history, and ticket store. Perform external research when a recovered decision relies on a community-practice claim that the transcript or repository cannot substantiate; otherwise label the claim transcript-only.\n- Recover later decisions and phase summaries to the extent supported, clearly labeling gaps and confidence.\n- Write `.joe-janitor/report-2026-08-16-recovered.md` with the recovery banner and record conclusions on this ticket.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each of decisions 1-6 has a recovered evidence record.\n- [ ] Each of decisions 1-6 states its recovered rationale.\n- [ ] Each of decisions 1-6 states its approval status.\n- [ ] Each of decisions 1-6 carries an explicit confidence or uncertainty label.\n- [ ] Claims in the report label their source as transcript, repository, tracker, or external research.\n- [ ] The report maps the current protocol’s five phases and labels any historical divergence or inferred mapping.\n- [ ] The report explicitly names missing phase outputs.\n- [ ] Existing decision-to-ticket mappings are listed without creating duplicate remediation tickets.\n- [ ] `.joe-janitor/report-2026-08-16-recovered.md` exists with the `RECOVERED — NOT A NATIVE JANITOR RUN` banner.\n- [ ] No production-code file is modified.\n- [ ] A ticket comment records the recovery conclusions and exact artifact path."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786897875327627001,"uuid":"e212dc76-cc10-4c03-a84a-de423b266c8f"}